The ODE system of the model {{ ("`" ~ model.id ~ "`") | julia_text if model.id else "without id" }}{% if model.name and model.name != model.id %}: {{ model.name | julia_text }}{% endif %}.

Written by sbmlutils {{ model.sbmlutils }}{% if model.source %} from {{ model.source | julia_text }}{% endif %}, SBML L{{ model.level }}V{{ model.version }}.
{% set units = [] %}
{% for key, unit in model.units.items() if unit %}
{% set _ = units.append([key, unit]) %}
{% endfor %}
{% if units %}

Units of the model:

{{ table(units, 4, julia_text) }}
{% endif %}
{% if states %}

States x:

{{ table([["", "id", "name", "unit"]] + rows(states, "index", "id", "name", "unit"), 4, julia_text) }}
{% endif %}

`initial_values(p)` returns the initial states x0 and the constants p at t = 0,
`f!(dx, x, p, t)` the rates of change of the states and `f_y(x, p, t)` the assigned
values y, the rules and the reaction rates.
{% if events %}
`EVENTS` lists the events with the functions of their delays, priorities and
assignments, `event_triggers(x, p, t)` and `event_conditions(x, p, t)` their triggers.
{% endif %}
{% if options.simulator %}
`simulate(t_end)` returns a `DataFrame` of a simulation with an integrator of
